From 97c060a10bf0d19cea4b163853ceb873ed431478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liushanshan <ss0217.liu@samsung.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:30:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Guard BOLT tool builds, process cleanup and installed clang
 security

Accept only the certified 110 llvm-bolt dry-run task descriptions with a
fixed English Ninja progress format. Reject unexpected install products,
invalid ELF ranges, stale or invalid tiny outputs and malformed tool versions.
Kill the entire command process group on failure and wait up to ten seconds
for all non-zombie members to exit. Preserve ELF security attributes after
full stripping and in the final RPM post gate.

Keep the candidate generation steps and BOLT options unchanged. Move BOLT-only
whitespace inside its conditionals so disabled build/install sections match
cb679968 byte for byte in debug and release macro chains.

Quickbuild build parameters and project configuration cannot be changed.
x86_64 therefore keeps %bcond_without clang_bolt (enabled by default).
--without clang_bolt is for local builds. To disable BOLT in Quickbuild,
submit a new spec commit changing x86_64 to %bcond_with clang_bolt.

Validation: 146 fixtures; ordinary/candidate ELF security preservation;
debug/release disabled-spec byte comparison; real tiny, post reverse,
compare-root and tool-plan gates. Candidate SHA remains 4ec07159.
No Gerrit branch is pushed by this validation task.
